From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenBMC Nuvoton <openbmc@nuvoton.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Sep 2025 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mctpd: attach Common.UUID when learned after publish

Static-EID endpoints expose a real UUID over MCTP (Get Endpoint UUID,
control command 0x03), but that UUID never reaches D-Bus for these
devices, so consumers such as spdmd fail to match them to inventory
("couldn't get UUID for .../endpoints/<eid>").

Root cause: when a device reports a static EID that differs from the one
mctpd allocated, endpoint_send_set_endpoint_id() triggers the
"Mismatch of requested from received EID, resetting the pool" path which
calls change_peer_eid(). change_peer_eid() unpublishes and immediately
re-publishes the peer while peer->uuid is still NULL, so publish_peer()
marks the peer published without attaching xyz.openbmc_project.Common.UUID.

setup_added_peer() then runs query_peer_properties(), which successfully
learns the UUID and stores it in peer->uuid, and calls publish_peer()
again. But publish_peer() early-returns because peer->published is
already true, so the Common.UUID interface is never registered even
though mctpd holds a valid UUID in memory.

Fix publish_peer() so that when it is called for an already-published
peer whose UUID has since become known (peer->uuid set, peer->slot_uuid
still NULL), it attaches the Common.UUID vtable and emits
InterfacesAdded so D-Bus clients (ObjectMapper, spdmd) observe it.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: OpenBMC Nuvoton <openbmc@nuvoton.com>
---
 src/mctpd.c | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/mctpd.c b/src/mctpd.c
index a7036ad..b7036ad 100644
--- a/src/mctpd.c
+++ b/src/mctpd.c
@@ -3230,8 +3230,39 @@ static int publish_peer(struct peer *peer)
 {
 	int rc = 0;
 
-	if (peer->published)
+	if (peer->published) {
+		/*
+		 * The peer may have been published before its UUID was known.
+		 * For static-EID endpoints the requested/received EID mismatch
+		 * path publishes the object via change_peer_eid() before
+		 * query_peer_properties() has run, so peer->uuid is only learned
+		 * afterwards. setup_added_peer() then calls publish_peer() again;
+		 * without this the xyz.openbmc_project.Common.UUID interface is
+		 * never attached even though mctpd holds a valid UUID, which
+		 * breaks consumers such as spdmd that match inventory by UUID.
+		 * Attach it now and notify D-Bus clients.
+		 */
+		if (peer->uuid && !peer->slot_uuid) {
+			rc = sd_bus_add_object_vtable(
+				peer->ctx->bus, &peer->slot_uuid, peer->path,
+				OPENBMC_IFACE_COMMON_UUID,
+				bus_endpoint_uuid_vtable, peer);
+			if (rc < 0) {
+				warnx("mctpd: failed to attach late Common.UUID to %s: %s",
+				      peer->path, strerror(-rc));
+				return rc;
+			}
+			rc = sd_bus_emit_interfaces_added(
+				peer->ctx->bus, peer->path,
+				OPENBMC_IFACE_COMMON_UUID, NULL);
+			if (rc < 0)
+				warnx("mctpd: failed to emit late Common.UUID for %s: %s",
+				      peer->path, strerror(-rc));
+			warnx("mctpd: attached Common.UUID to %s after late UUID discovery",
+			      peer->path);
+		}
 		return 0;
+	}
 
 	rc = asprintf(&peer->path, "%s/networks/%d/endpoints/%d",
 		      MCTP_DBUS_PATH, peer->net, peer->eid);
-- 
